{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802019-preventing-frenzy","id":802019,"title":"Preventing Frenzy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-06T05:45:48-08:00","id":802019,"title":"Preventing Frenzy?","content":"I'm playing a game of experienced ancillae/newly Elder characters. Mine is essentially built to be the Domain's Hound. Kindred Duelling is a good way to display she's meant to fight other vampires, as opposed to the various other things a vampire might fight, but I have one problem:<br /> <br /> There are many ways to force a Frenzy on someone. Cruac, Kindred Dueling, chucking a molotov, whatever.<br /> <br /> How do you keep the Elder Ordo Dracul who has mastered the Mystery of the Wyrm from frenzying and just wrecking everything and everyone? This is something a Hound would have to keep in mind, I assume.<br /> <br /> Less drastic examples are also welcome, but this particular one is an active concern. She's Crone, but any options are available just for my personal knowledge. Discipline, devotion, ritual, merit, core power, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":".  Wrong Covenant 01-06-2016, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T07:39:50-08:00","id":802090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802019-preventing-frenzy#post802019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you keep the Elder Ordo Dracul who has mastered the Mystery of the Wyrm from frenzying and just wrecking everything and everyone? This is something a Hound would have to keep in mind, I assume.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you've mastered Wyrm... you don't. You get to set whatever your frenzy goal is with Wyrm. So, lets say someone forces you to frenzy. You set &quot;Use Predator Aura to cow the offender&quot; as your goal, you get huge bonuses to do it, and then you slip out of frenzy when you acomplish your goal.<br /> <br /> Someone tries to mind control you, you slip into controlled frenzy, negating the mind control, then slip out of it when you've acomplished your goal.<br /> <br /> Mystery of the Wyrm is there to ride the wave at a moment's notice and abuse all the benefits while remaining in control of your actions. You don't worry about holding it in check. You ride it like a horse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T08:10:20-08:00","id":802107,"title":"","content":"I think they meant keeping <i>other</i> ordo dracul members in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T08:12:26-08:00","id":802108,"title":"","content":"<b>New Devotion<br /> Leash the Beast</b><br /> (Animalism <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, </b>Vigor \u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Animalism allows one to incite bestial rage and vampiric frenzy. This Devotion turns it around, leashing another vampire\u2019s Beast with the Predatory Aura, allowing the user to force them into docility whether the affected Kindred wants it or not. It either keeps them from frenzying at all or ends a frenzy they are in.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Poo</b>l: Presence + Intimidation + Animalism vs. Resolve + Blood Potency (if resisted)<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Scene<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The vampire fails to leash the Beast and is incited herself. She immediately frenzies with the goal of subduing the original target or fleeing from him.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure</b>: The vampire fails to leash the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Success</b>: The target becomes unable to frenzy for the rest of the Scene. A frenzying vampire immediately exits Frenzy. Furthermore, the affected character takes a penalty equal to the user\u2019s Vigor on rolls to use the Predatory Aura for the rest of the Scene. Any supernatural powers that force frenzy must first win a Clash of Wills against this power.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: As above and the target becomes unable to use the Predatory Aura for the Scene. Any attempts to lash out against him are uncontested.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 3 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>New Merit</b><br /> <b>Beast Tamer</b> <b>(Style, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022?)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite: </b>Animalism \u2022, Wits <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022, </b>Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> The character is experienced or trained in dealing with vampires in the throes of Frenzy. She knows how to move to avoid harm or make them attack with less force. The best have learned how to reign in a rampaging vampire, allowing them to tame a frenzying vampire like an undead beast tamer.<br /> <br /> <b>Know the Beast (\u2022): </b>The character has an instinctual understanding of the way a frenzying vampire moves and attacks. When a frenzying vampire attacks the character, reduce the bonus from Frenzy on the Attack roll by the character\u2019s Animalism down to a minimum of 0.<br /> <br /> <b>Survive the Onslaught (\u2022\u2022): </b>The character\u2019s skill at staying unharmed against a frenzying opponent has grown keener. When he has a chance to focus he evades with surprising finesse. When spending Willpower to increase his Defense, increase his Defense by +4 instead of +2 against frenzying opponents. When Dodging, a Willpower point grants +4 and 8-again on the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Soothe the Beast (\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Now that he knows how to survive, he can use his understanding to diffuse the Beast\u2019s rage through psychological tricks. After a successful Dodge the character can attempt a reflexive Social Roll appropriate to the situation. Successes on this roll are treated as if they came from a Touchstone trying to talk down the frenzying character (see pg. 104, Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition).<br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from these, I could imagine similar Cr\u00faac and Theban Sorcery Rituals. Since you say your character is Ordo, how about developing a Scale of the Wyrm that deals with this?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Edit</u>: </b>Thinking about it, you might want to trade the effects of the first and second dot. Also, you could add a third dot (pushing Soothe the Beast to fourth) that is about using Social Rolls to change the goal of the Frenzy mid-Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Added a thought 01-06-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T10:03:06-08:00","id":802190,"title":"","content":"@MCN Apologies if I was unclear. The primary question I am asking here is how to prevent a Vampire from entering into Frenzy. The Ordo Dracul is just an extreme example of why such a thing might be necessary.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar272_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"272\" data-vbnamecard=\"272\">saibot</a> Are those homebrewed? Or from an upcoming book? As a player in this circumstance, I can't really do homebrew stuff, but they do look interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T10:09:19-08:00","id":802195,"title":"","content":"They are indeed homebrewed. If supernatural powers are not an option, things get tricky. No way to stop someone with the Coil of the Wyrm, for others consider the Frenzy modifiers. Just make sure the things that give penalties are not applicable, while those that are bonuses are true. Be non-threatening, arrange for good feeding, have trusted neutral ground.<br /> <br /> Narratively, you might even take it on you as a Hound to teach &quot;Frenzy Prevention Strategies&quot; to the young and perhaps earn some City Status that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T10:56:02-08:00","id":802221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802019-preventing-frenzy?p=802190#post802190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MCN Apologies if I was unclear. The primary question I am asking here is how to prevent a Vampire from entering into Frenzy. The Ordo Dracul is just an extreme example of why such a thing might be necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div> In that case, I suggest learning Animalism. There's a devotion for protecting Elysium grounds that give bonuses to that.<br /> <br /> Use Dominate. You can't get the elder to stop, but you can redirect them to do something harmless. Maybe convince them to be hungry and take a bite out of your arm isntead. They'll calm down after feeding.<br /> <br /> But if they already fell into frenzy... you don't magically stop it. Frezny is supposed to be SCARY. Vampire Elysium's rules are built to keep that predator in check, because you never know when someone will snap. Having a power that suddenly ends the frenzy ruins the drama of it. When someone frenzies, you just have to be better than them. Using the upcoming Crone FS and lots of Celerity and Resilience helps alot. Dodge action, reduce their dice pool to zero, keep all the attention on yourself while protecting everyone else.<br /> <br /> EDIT - you're not supposed to stop a frenzying elder. You can only survive it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-06-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T11:36:30-08:00","id":802243,"title":"","content":"Wait, so you're trying to prevent other vampires from Frenzying? The only means I'm aware of are preventative measures. The Reason's Salon Devotion gives everyone in the area bonuses to resist Frenzy. The Chapterhouse Merit in the Secrets of the Covenants Ordo preview does something similar. Once a vampire has started Frenzying though, the only things that will stop them are getting what they want, their Touchstone talking them down, a stake to the heart, torpor, or final death. That's why I always specialize my Sheriffs and Hounds for staking, so they have a non-lethal way to deal with a Frenzy situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T12:20:35-08:00","id":802262,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I meant that she is Crone. I edited the OP to reflect that.<br /> <br /> And yes, prevention is the goal. After it starts, it's certainly too late to stop it.<br /> <br /> Staking is a very good idea. I don't know why I didn't think of that.<br /> <br /> The redirecting ideas were good, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T12:35:34-08:00","id":802270,"title":"","content":"If the intentions is to PREVENT and not to stop, with Majesty (Green Eyes) you should be able to modify the emotions at your will (if you win the contested roll), so I think you should be able to calm down the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T13:11:05-08:00","id":802296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/802019-preventing-frenzy?p=802108#post802108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]<br /> <b>Know the Beast (\u2022): </b>The character has an instinctual understanding of the way a frenzying vampire moves and attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of the instinctual vampiric spider-sense combat style Anne Rice vampires can use. I always wanted to introduce that idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T13:31:57-08:00","id":802307,"title":"","content":"Too bad you aren't a Ghoul or mortal!<br /> <br /> Beast Whispers (p. 300) would let you talk down <i>any</i> Kindred that frenzies, regardless of whether or not you are their Touchstone. Alternatively, a mortal or Ghoul with Beloved (p. 300) who acts as someone's Touchstone has solid benefits vis-a-vis stopping and preventing Frenzy.<br /> <br /> If you can find (or request) a Ghoul with Beast Whispers and can Blood Bond them... just cart them around and use them to knock people out of Frenzy. Are you Daeva, by any chance? Give the Ghoul Majesty for the raw bonus to Presence rolls, and they can score the (potentially 30) Successes needed to talk them out of Frenzy all the easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T13:33:28-08:00","id":802310,"title":"","content":"Is the creative casting system from Sacriments and Blasphemies on the table? I imagine you could create a Protection ritual to ward against Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T13:52:03-08:00","id":802325,"title":"","content":"Finding ghouls might be tricky, but an opportunity to take if it becomes possible. I'm not sure if there are ways to 'tank' so to speak, so they may just die before they get to use it...<br /> <br /> S&amp;B is being used. I'll have to look at what level that's possible. Can't be used in combat, but the goal is prevention, so that's another good possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:18:26-08:00","id":802423,"title":"","content":"Someone give Saibot a freelancer job, those merits and devotion are tiiiiiiiight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}